Rant if they had asked -- you have my permission

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.320
to use this video.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:14.020
“And one more note of those mechanical sounds
she hears. The Invisible Man doesn't really have

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:18.370
a signature sound like some of the other classic
Universal monsters. You can't have him growl

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:22.010
like the Wolfman or hiss like Dracula, cause
that would be ridiculous, so it's cool how

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:26.529
they found a sound that fits the sci-fi reimagining
of the story and is also still really creepy.”

00:13:26.529 --> 00:13:31.180
“The Invisible Man is a classic horror villain,
but he struggles to be as recognizable as

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:35.890
some other antagonists. Unlike the moan of
Frankenstein’s monster or the howl of The

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:40.990
Wolfman, this version of The Invisible Man
is associated with a mechanical kind of sound.

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:46.350
So in a way, this Invisible Man does have
a signature sound and it ties into the technology

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:47.980
that makes him so creepy.”

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:52.510
Why did you even steal that? That was just a side
note that I said. I didn’t even count that

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:55.720
as one of my Things You Missed. You’re just
making a fool of yourself now Screen Rant.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.830
But sadly, I don’t think Screen Rant is
the only company guilty of ripping off YouTubers.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:04.470
It’s kind of a disturbing trend. Just this
week I saw a video by gaming documentarian

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:08.589
Slush, who had his most popular video ripped
off a year later by The Score eSports. By

00:14:08.589 --> 00:14:12.779
the look of things it was the same kind of
deal, just take the script, reword certain

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:16.460
things, remove any semblance of personality,
add something that makes you look like a dumb***

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:18.519
and publish it, acting like it’s your creation.

00:14:18.519 --> 00:14:22.111
If it doesn’t seem like a huge deal, just
try to remember that for independent YouTube

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:27.820
creators like me, Jon Solo, Slush and many
others, this is our job, this is our livelihood.

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:32.680
I’m a baker selling cakes in a town of 400K,
and Screen Rant is taking my cakes, slapping

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.560
on a different colored frosting and selling
them in my town and seventeen others.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.620
Like I said, I think I’m being reasonable
to ask that they say something along the lines

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:45.640
of, “CZsWorld made a video where talks about
how these scenes are similar to scenes directed

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:50.790
by Oren Peli and James Wan. If you want to
watch that there’s a link in the description.”

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.810
That’s the other thing about these channels.
Why do they always sound like they’re constantly

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.620
saying the same run-on sentence.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.590
Hey and that goes for you people putting stuff
from my videos on IMDb too. I saw one the

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:03.161
other day when I accidentally said the words
“hydrochloric acid” in my video, when

00:15:03.161 --> 00:15:06.800
it should have been “hydrofluoric acid”.
And someone had just kind of transcribed all

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.500
my points into trivia bits on IMDb and they
wrote “hydrochloric”. Like they didn’t

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.500
even both to check if it was correct.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:16.100
Anyway, I’ll put the contact email and the
Twitter information for Screen Rant if anyone

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:19.959
wants to let them know how you feel about
this. I think I said it best in my video about

00:15:19.959 --> 00:15:23.810
The Invisible Man, when I compared the character
Adrian’s practices to the lyrics sung by

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.700
Long Island emo band, Brand New:

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.280
“Everyone’s
caught on, to everything you do.”

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:31.800
I'll see you in the next one. Assuming we both
survive.

